#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8462488e-272b-5772-bf64-9aa1638edb21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466405} {:answer/id #uuid "06728173-b51c-55c4-92d8-9851289d57bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06728173-b51c-55c4-92d8-9851289d57bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466406} :answer-field/id #uuid "caa1bd4a-3eba-56e1-a3ba-6e63da10f9e6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467046} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc57e6f5-5ce9-51db-a506-35f8fe3453e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466407} {:answer/id #uuid "634f6c08-51bc-5474-b7ad-cca79735d829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "634f6c08-51bc-5474-b7ad-cca79735d829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466408} :answer-field/id #uuid "e33b4fc0-086e-5fab-be31-3e3d8f7b2025" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467047} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e38e3054-6ed9-56c7-8585-41217d71f832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466409} {:answer/id #uuid "1168cf38-73e5-5de7-a26b-6306956051c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1168cf38-73e5-5de7-a26b-6306956051c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466410} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a51316-22f5-5b3e-9744-bdf00aa12c02" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a6ed137-ea67-591f-bf1a-a0d1b0037ea7" :question/math-academy-id "q-337778" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{1}{x+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,y$\n\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)=\\sqrt{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y$\n\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{e}^{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,y$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x},{f}_{1}(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-2.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)=2,{f}_{2}(x)={e}^{x},{f}_{1}(x)=0,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c09d354a-972a-5465-a370-382725d7b170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466411} {:answer/id #uuid "931baba1-25ba-5aa4-838d-d4d1a6ee68e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "931baba1-25ba-5aa4-838d-d4d1a6ee68e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466412} :answer-field/id #uuid "102e6fe5-9125-5537-a52b-b0aeb5de1c77" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467049} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a393e95a-e314-51d1-99d7-34e17cd38f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466413} {:answer/id #uuid "fec6c785-e394-5d5a-9a52-7bfe59d63811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a393e95a-e314-51d1-99d7-34e17cd38f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466413} :answer-field/id #uuid "791eec01-b9c2-5df9-942e-0daf202a70bb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467050} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee40cac9-7a57-5fac-b22a-c406ca0af7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466415} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbb0027-90e5-5d9b-a0e0-9efdc9f79150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee40cac9-7a57-5fac-b22a-c406ca0af7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466415} :answer-field/id #uuid "e85b61ba-147a-5912-8b88-b495aa1835d5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5914278-adab-5478-b262-9e2341a90a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-338102" :question/problem "Which of the following second-order differential equations are linear?\n- **I.** $x{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}$\n- **II.** $y{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x$\n- **III.** $5{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+7{y}^{2}=x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "А second-order linear differential equation has the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nLet's look at each equation in turn.\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+y={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis a second-order linear ODE with $a(x)=x,b(x)=0,c(x)=1,$ and $f(x)={x}^{2}.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\ny{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $y{y}^{″}.$\n\n- The equation \n\n$$\n5{y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+7{y}^{2}=x\n$$\n\nis **NOT** linear because it contains the nonlinear term $7{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "537e9287-d40b-541a-a771-35fdebb7a68e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466417} {:answer/id #uuid "b86f20e9-e99e-5043-a105-41ba0d06d907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "537e9287-d40b-541a-a771-35fdebb7a68e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466417} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee149c43-cd32-54e1-88b1-1a761ba1088d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56ff9540-7748-56d0-8dcc-17c53b286037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466419} {:answer/id #uuid "99c15a2b-52b5-5f4f-a9bd-e392ccd7dd01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56ff9540-7748-56d0-8dcc-17c53b286037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466419} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbafeabb-acd0-55ae-b50b-63a06106240a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71c453fc-3161-5efe-87c9-b5487086f7eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466421} {:answer/id #uuid "d3699871-4a43-5354-8111-f56a66a66074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3699871-4a43-5354-8111-f56a66a66074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466422} :answer-field/id #uuid "31b0a69c-b01a-51bf-ad6d-bd58d94109aa" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1c5937c-0d4d-5848-8380-65f08dc10e61" :question/math-academy-id "q-338104" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n- **I.** ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- **II.** ${D}_{2}(y)=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y)\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+y$\n- **III.** ${D}_{3}(y)=(1+{x}^{2})\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}y$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y),$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is $x\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y),$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=1+{x}^{2},{f}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x),$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Initial Value Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a39e901-0aa1-5d86-b708-0e8acb2ac5d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466423} {:answer/id #uuid "29e4116f-8a15-53fe-9ea6-b1b9dad75542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a39e901-0aa1-5d86-b708-0e8acb2ac5d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466423} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9207047-339f-5590-b907-7f7c565f9552" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467055} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "865dc4fa-d649-5eb9-a7ec-5bde925f9d64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466425} {:answer/id #uuid "dcaaf4f2-b503-5bf6-83a4-be3c5e2cef67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcaaf4f2-b503-5bf6-83a4-be3c5e2cef67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466426} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c825d3a-0580-5864-b085-36ece98d3299" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467056} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6959ade9-49ae-5973-9caa-620065c11d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466427} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc34701-51c2-57e9-8294-7861a2a09033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466428}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6959ade9-49ae-5973-9caa-620065c11d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466427} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6b83349-428f-55e7-acb7-eb348ac4f370" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dabe6837-4031-5ea3-85c8-7a53d65944dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-338531" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}-3{y}^{′}+y={e}^{x},\\,y(0)=1,\\,y(2)=0$\n- **II.** ${y}^{″}+4y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-1$\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}-y={x}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$).\n\n- The third system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Initial Value Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6836982-f6d8-52f8-815d-9525a8903655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466429} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0a38e7-67c6-52ec-be17-5586868af018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6836982-f6d8-52f8-815d-9525a8903655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466429} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f230617-a629-5dbf-9fa6-42a16dd6c5bc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04973466-3738-5bff-b1f2-ace9af564b53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466431} {:answer/id #uuid "0e8e13eb-9e6f-58ad-a231-0486e26e30f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04973466-3738-5bff-b1f2-ace9af564b53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466431} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2885e5d-2c03-53c7-bc3d-19f929c42aac" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467059} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fe77deb-cfc5-5881-8d56-96c7bcafedbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466433} {:answer/id #uuid "a39275f9-b508-525c-a97a-9587ce4361a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a39275f9-b508-525c-a97a-9587ce4361a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466434} :answer-field/id #uuid "750c2223-91a4-5d91-ae4f-93359625a42b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce074393-6c5e-5e9b-ab9a-92fd971d7d06" :question/math-academy-id "q-338533" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,y(0)=2,\\,y(5)=2$\n- **II.** ${y}^{″}+y={x}^{3}$\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(-3)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-3)=1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=5$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-3$)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34d342c-e7fc-581b-b3d1-ed6a49f1a62f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Boundary Value Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "974d1fce-aeff-5a83-83a9-3bb949b0b70e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466435} {:answer/id #uuid "f12d0b9d-f226-5f1e-921e-a2e48e09c132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f12d0b9d-f226-5f1e-921e-a2e48e09c132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466436} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a94a6a-2f69-53fa-a9e6-34196f225ae9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467061} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f35c850d-c1a9-584f-a83f-87a191d132f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466437} {:answer/id #uuid "b24ecf5b-36cf-5b0e-8368-d96e6ec4f971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f35c850d-c1a9-584f-a83f-87a191d132f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466437} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4dcb98-f97f-55f2-b121-2ec454e144d4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467062} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b4228a-972b-519e-82fb-ff14ba5edf19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466439} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdff215-582b-5015-9ef0-1daeadbb8820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b4228a-972b-519e-82fb-ff14ba5edf19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466439} :answer-field/id #uuid "4895eabd-bc6d-5404-b330-29fb8fd463ee" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fcfd17f-1887-5fc2-a463-d8fe70a76b3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-338539" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}+y=x{e}^{x},\\,y(0)=3,\\,y(4)=3$\n- **II.** ${y}^{″}-y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+4y=0,\\,y(-2)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(-2)=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=4$).\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is not a boundary value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the *same* location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-2$). This is an **initial value problem.**"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34d342c-e7fc-581b-b3d1-ed6a49f1a62f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Boundary Value Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52d9ab04-27e8-5354-8977-b0a649439b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466441} {:answer/id #uuid "93bf8183-22b5-5724-ae04-6c0e1324eff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93bf8183-22b5-5724-ae04-6c0e1324eff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466442} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a11f77-da8e-5e83-ac52-17ba64d85033" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467064} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "297318f6-bb6f-57cc-9859-55fdde57c577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466443} {:answer/id #uuid "b40930ce-93c8-5904-9ee7-8a18cebac545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "297318f6-bb6f-57cc-9859-55fdde57c577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466443} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3aca6ca-5ece-5763-a9f3-1047c04c1116" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467065} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e46af8b-a46a-5014-bbbf-decdab105038" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466445} {:answer/id #uuid "53785e33-0269-55bd-b69a-e85f540eafb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53785e33-0269-55bd-b69a-e85f540eafb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466446} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ad4734-bba5-5ef8-8fb0-8777b499b1a2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4fd4473-8c46-5808-aedb-c06540dd956d" :question/math-academy-id "q-338595" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a boundary value problem?\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}-y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\,y(0)=1,\\,y(2)=0$\n- **II.** $3{y}^{″}-y={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=4$\n- **III.** ${y}^{″}+y={x}^{2},\\,y(-1)=2,\\,y(1)=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at *different* locations in the domain of $y,$ then this is a **boundary value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=2$).\n\n- The second system is not a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation combined with only one condition.\n\n- The third system is a boundary value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-1$ and $x=1$)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Initial Value Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f592f822-6479-5a95-8a4e-6c1b3c5df430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466447} {:answer/id #uuid "b81c1845-e481-57c6-8f8e-7b6c5cc2f4bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f592f822-6479-5a95-8a4e-6c1b3c5df430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466447} :answer-field/id #uuid "29186b36-9a37-50dc-94f5-c88938def68c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9b50c31-5f22-5daf-8314-57ac0f9cae41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466449} {:answer/id #uuid "aa873f68-4443-5c44-90f7-3d07645d556f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17