_{1}(t)-8{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5))^{2}{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is not a first-order linear system of ODEs since it contains the term ${x}_{1}(t){x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- System II is not a first-order linear system of ODEs since it contains the term ${x}_{1}^{2}(t).$\n\n- System III is a first-order linear system of ODEs since it can be written in the standard form, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=3, &  & b(t)=-8, &  & f(t)=0, \\\\ c(t)=1, &  & d(t)=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)^{2}, &  & g(t)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314812 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous and Inhomogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d8056b2-2a73-571e-b455-5dc959eab75c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467094} {:answer/id #uuid "19066ca7-4b35-5bbc-916c-8942673e263a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19066ca7-4b35-5bbc-916c-8942673e263a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/