-ebb00a836540" :question/math-academy-id "q-339658" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- **II.** ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- **III.** ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "In matrix form, the system\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=A(t)x(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nis *homogeneous* when $f≡0,$ and *inhomogeneous* when $f≢0.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\n- System II is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous and Inhomogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1015030b-9dc0-59b2-a199-21b03bef2718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467100} {:answer/id #uuid "dad9ffc4-12f0-5fc1-8c72-3d4ee6a0f268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dad9ffc4-12f0-5fc1-8c72-3d4ee6a0f268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467101} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9296136-c645-521c-bb63-058fcb9fb89f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468271} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc6ff9dd-fc2a-5843-b3ab-ccf4bd747718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467102} {:answer/id #uuid "23f6e380-4c79-579b-b150-cf88da4be31d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc6ff9dd-fc2a-5843-b3ab-ccf4bd747718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467102} :answer-field/id #uuid "62dd4ee5-9236-5331-bfce-b54dc70ce367" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee1db27a-8cf0-5d9f-913b-65c9cfe20dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467104} {:answer/id #uuid "a38f52e9-6ce3-5221-abc9-ff0f3f37ad65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee1db27a-8cf0-5d9f-913b-65c9cfe20dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467104} :answer-field/id #uuid "071b0070-7425-5216-8e73-bfe46c1f5725" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d86591cd-cf9c-5b7c-ab46-ee83fbeda055" :question/math-academy-id "q-339661" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- **II.** ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- **III.** ${x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "In matrix form, the system\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=A(t)x(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nis *homogeneous* when $f≡0,$ and *inhomogeneous* when $f≢0.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since $f≡0.$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since $f=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]≢0.$\n\n- System III is inhomogeneous since $f=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}]≢0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous and Inhomogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "899117d7-db47-58c1-8b04-71ff13db84ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467106} {:answer/id #uuid "c51319a9-62aa-53bf-977b-1b28d347c8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c51319a9-62aa-53bf-977b-1b28d347c8d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467107} :answer-field/id #uuid "7811e01e-7754-5558-a044-86b309427f20" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea6cd620-ed14-54e4-8d80-41ebc61e1d4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467108} {:answer/id #uuid "934a6947-dd5d-54b5-bf56-c18d89fefdaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea6cd620-ed14-54e4-8d80-41ebc61e1d4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467108} :answer-field/id #uuid "26240d32-05e4-5a29-bd70-9c4756fb5be2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468275} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46c0bc7d-9227-55bc-b43d-05893caeff18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467110} {:answer/id #uuid "255a0fd0-e3a2-5794-a709-e0ee7f3d415d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "255a0fd0-e3a2-5794-a709-e0ee7f3d415d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467111} :answer-field/id #uuid "0319c04f-0988-5a05-98de-dc9e795cbf20" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a032209-c882-5496-a788-3681657f5173" :question/math-academy-id "q-339663" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- **II.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+t\\end{aligned}$\n- **III.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of the form\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f≡0$ and $g≡0$ (i.e., both $f$ and $g$ are zero functions), then the system is *homogeneous*. Otherwise, if at least one of $f$ or $g$ is not identically zero, the system is *inhomogeneous*.\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-2, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=4, &  & d(t)=-1, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=1, &  & b(t)=2, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=0, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147494 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "680a42fd-9b70-5fb2-916c-d10b71b11d82" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using Phase Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd5d1cb6-e199-580c-964c-f58e2baa63bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467112} {:answer/id #uuid "277f535c-16ef-54af-8b7d-e81c5749e8af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "277f535c-16ef-54af-8b7d-e81c5749e8af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467113} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc470065-516f-572e-9f72-f7abb557c927" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468277} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0caac1f0-6eed-56ca-8cfa-00c7633f3279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467114} {:answer/id #uuid "c719ca97-b102-5ea7-8ddd-536c3accc698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c719ca97-b102-5ea7-8ddd-536c3accc698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467115} :answer-field/id #uuid "912fb887-4b94-5a44-9c6c-0810845699a7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdc68df-95d2-52ab-952b-1357ad5a0267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467116} {:answer/id #uuid "f18d429d-8012-5c35-ae3b-7e9257605def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bdc68df-95d2-52ab-952b-1357ad5a0267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467116} :answer-field/id #uuid "7922cd17-8535-522c-a0bc-57d40cb0ca61" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b869e45a-6b1f-53e1-aacc-10ffe2baaefd" :question/math-academy-id "q-339664" :question/problem "![](images/52/528bf1bc9d6177f031b8b5504641903a11dfc2c2576e4759bf4cb7c278d0585c.png)\n\nA particular autonomous differential equation has the phase line shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $y=0$ is a sink\n\nII. $y=3$ is a source\n\nIII. $y=3$ is a node\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=0$ points downward, and the arrow just below it points upward. In other words, both arrows point *toward* the point $y=0.$ This means that $y=0$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. Notice that the arrow just above the point $y=3$ points upward, and the arrow just below it points downward. In other words, both arrows point *away* from $y=3.$ This means that $y=3$ is a source.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous and Inhomogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84e9a197-043d-551c-8891-0c6e67096641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467118} {:answer/id #uuid "fca57084-6fd8-5f4c-b99e-8c15f967fe6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84e9a197-043d-551c-8891-0c6e67096641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467118} :answer-field/id #uuid "13a2eb2c-5896-5c07-ac0d-431d3b73188a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468280} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b01efb9-ead7-5710-8335-7337723cfc50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467120} {:answer/id #uuid "412b45e1-738d-598e-819e-f952927c1178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b01efb9-ead7-5710-8335-7337723cfc50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467120} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeda461c-ac53-5d3a-83bf-6523881e961a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468281} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74efcba8-a58e-5c07-b037-ec950946d142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467122} {:answer/id #uuid "1f78cfe5-c4ab-5be4-a1b5-cd6cf3707a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f78cfe5-c4ab-5be4-a1b5-cd6cf3707a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467123} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a9bc416-d800-5e5c-a0a0-d0c366981716" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "834c59a7-4f2c-54c0-913b-f196a907cc0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339669" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)+2{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}$\n- **II.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)+4{e}^{t} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- **III.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-4{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5){x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of the form\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f≡0$ and $g≡0$ (i.e., both $f$ and $g$ are zero functions), then the system is *homogeneous*. Otherwise, if at least one of $f$ or $g$ is not identically zero, the system is *inhomogeneous*.\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≢0$ and $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-3, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6t) \\\\ c(t)=1, &  & d(t)=-2, &  & g(t)=2{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=1, &  & b(t)=3, &  & f(t)=4{e}^{t} \\\\ c(t)=1, &  & d(t)=-1, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-4, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=1, &  & d(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5), &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129316 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28939f65-9fd6-564d-a0c2-73c1038ac898" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Homogeneous and Inhomogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a16b4af-a3c6-52be-9017-ad0ff1124280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467124} {:answer/id #uuid "a4a091fe-c72f-5f93-9d2b-1f06e62d6afc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a16b4af-a3c6-52be-9017-ad0ff1124280" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467124} :answer-field/id #uuid "c96620b0-a25e-53c9-addc-4724bc41e2fb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bae1c72d-b801-5e76-b195-593b182a757e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467126} {:answer/id #uuid "71b25915-a547-5dea-8e7d-6ef8de74b585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71b25915-a547-5dea-8e7d-6ef8de74b585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467127} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd3d80f-1d80-5b15-9c50-2481adf059bc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6ad4a64-2d4c-5a05-935d-21b75b394c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467128} {:answer/id #uuid "73396a32-eb81-5b5d-8986-0369cb82f7b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6ad4a64-2d4c-5a05-935d-21b75b394c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467128} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e315c1f-d9bb-5594-a4f3-b6684053e206" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6099dfb-5cd3-520d-98c0-7759f4ae7ca2" :question/math-academy-id "q-339672" :question/problem "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+1\\end{aligned}$\n- **II.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=5{x}_{1}(t)+6{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- **III.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)+{e}^{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)+3t\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of the form\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $f≡0$ and $g≡0$ (i.e., both $f$ and $g$ are zero functions), then the system is *homogeneous*. Otherwise, if at least one of $f$ or $g$ is not identically zero, the system is *inhomogeneous*.\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≢0$ and $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=3, &  & b(t)=2, &  & f(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5t) \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=4, &  & g(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is homogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≡0$ and $g≡0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=-1, &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0 \\\\ c(t)=5, &  & d(t)=6, &  & g(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is inhomogeneous since it can be written in the standard form with $f≢0$ and $g≢0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=4, &  & b(t)=0, &  & f(t)={e}^{2} \\\\ c(t)=0, &  & d(t)=1, &  & g(t)=3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147495 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d4aa2f9-e7d6-5b1e-b60d-28de95c6f268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467130} {:answer/id #uuid "a80bdaeb-8477-5e25-8f98-e68030f429f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d4aa2f9-e7d6-5b1e-b60d-28de95c6f268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467130} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a62476-6939-5f4a-a93e-be2044213f4b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468286} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24dc8c3f-fbe5-5945-aa47-d5863466c80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467132} {:answer/id #uuid "d41f7d92-8bb0-5d75-8a17-23b5ce756f85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d41f7d92-8bb0-5d75-8a17-23b5ce756f85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467133} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb306eb6-4759-53f8-82c1-4985ea358ad4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468287} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d95286-cc9a-577c-8ab6-e64237a81ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467134} {:answer/id #uuid "1552cf16-b753-5c78-87aa-9c4684b6e64d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1552cf16-b753-5c78-87aa-9c4684b6e64d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467135} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2ea294b-3682-55bf-a782-e42fd07612b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb8d059f-7809-5041-a8a8-a0657d861dc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-339707" :question/problem "![](images/21/21970ba0ad8ae32ea95ad4f253d7be63aefe90316415f1aebad15c1fb3ccfd25.png)\n\nConsider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=1$ is a node.\n- $y=1$ is a sink.\n- $y=-3$ is a source.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/ec/eca3b223699f18fbb09c6657708b7680c4228f52323018168202351820360d9d.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=1$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-3$ is a source.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147495 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ff06b7a-7fe6-52db-ad53-7111896b7d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467136} {:answer/id #uuid "e99840a3-e258-5134-8b61-fc583c77dec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ff06b7a-7fe6-52db-ad53-7111896b7d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467136} :a