-field/id #uuid "cd49c2fb-b74c-5701-921e-2021a40da2cf" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12109bd9-1ea8-5fd9-b15c-ba4373902b35" :question/math-academy-id "q-37383" :question/problem "Which of the numbers below belong to  ${Q}_{0}^{+}?$\n- **I.** $0$\n- **II.** $\\sqrt{27}$\n- **III.** $-\\sqrt{4}$\n- **IV.** $\\frac{1}{9}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${Q}_{0}^{+}$ is the set of all positive rational numbers and $0.$\n\n- $0$ belongs to ${Q}_{0}^{+}.\\,✓$\n\n- $\\sqrt{27}=3\\sqrt{3}$ is not a rational number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}_{0}^{+}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $-\\sqrt{4}=-2$ is a negative number, so it does *not* belong to ${Q}_{0}^{+}.\\,\\times $\n\n- $\\frac{1}{9}$ is a rational number because it is the ratio of two integers, and moreover, it is a positive rational number. Therefore, $\\frac{1}{9}$ belongs to ${Q}_{0}^{+}.\\,✓$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and IV only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124528 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a6c0cf-04d4-5908-a03f-1adf491b9282" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f09b1c-9964-5ae6-9322-bf6de2b57681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467398} {:answer/id #uuid "dd858fdf-4fbe-5af0-b7f7-3d32c5fc5ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd858fdf-4fbe-5af0-b7f7-3d32c5fc5ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467399} :answer-field/id #uuid "e939d814-ae4b-507f-b423-19079a26ac60" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468420} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2758e74-ea85-5f56-a8cf-c1056f59c3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467400} {:answer/id #uuid "e83bbd17-0d14-5570-83ce-8018039ac54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e83bbd17-0d14-5570-83ce-8018039ac54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467401} :answer-field/id #uuid "6089e5b4-5b31-5cc3-8e8f-3c2b0ef217f0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3adb0444-ee54-507e-bc74-75995133eade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467402} {:answer/id #uuid "e35df19c-c12d-5884-9bab-6220a82bac4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3adb0444-ee54-507e-bc74-75995133eade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467402} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfa1370c-c573-5558-8a76-57bd2125c1c9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26a6234c-3080-57fe-a159-1f4332413072" :question/math-academy-id "q-37527" :question/problem "If $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix, then which of the following could be the characteristic equation of $B?$\n- **I.** ${\\lambda }^{3}-3{\\lambda }^{2}+1=0$\n- **II.** $(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +5)=0$\n- **III.** ${\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda =0$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ is invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, $0$ can't be an eigenvalue of $B.$ As a result, $\\lambda =0$ should not be a solution to the corresponding characteristic equation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given equations in turn.\n\n- Equation I could  be the characteristic equation of $B.$ Indeed, $\\lambda =0$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Equation II could be the characteristic equation of $B.$ Indeed, $\\lambda =0$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Equation III **cannot** be the characteristic equation of $B$ since $\\lambda =0$ is a root of the equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65112821-7bee-5d65-9072-8d6df8efb997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467404} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d25dfc-3ea3-5c6f-a70a-c04b8cb587f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65112821-7bee-5d65-9072-8d6df8efb997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467404} :answer-field/id #uuid "08a64ff2-0f5c-592a-a694-96380d251f4f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468423} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7b22f46-00f3-5f71-8433-0e28bd44d4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467406} {:answer/id #uuid "a910c191-586f-52d0-bc58-2320ce2cc779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a910c191-586f-52d0-bc58-2320ce2cc779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467407} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec8a870-a660-5ca5-87da-e92722d29f6d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee5ac67-1f2f-5723-8699-c4b5f9b6a498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467408} {:answer/id #uuid "4a6697d9-9225-5cba-a043-0834dae41039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ee5ac67-1f2f-5723-8699-c4b5f9b6a498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467408} :answer-field/id #uuid "108e3dce-9c13-5825-b131-e2991330ae58" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2437419d-408f-504c-b75e-afb16e745cc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-38355" :question/problem "![](images/71/718dd1f38f7c790ab83639f69462b372de6b7e8501c0a4d6ff678340ab4154bd.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=0$\n- The function is continuous at $x=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false.  The function is not left-continuous at $x=0,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=3\\ne 0=f(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=0,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)=0=f(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=0,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005e3900-6b8d-5e21-aabf-447866db29b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467410} {:answer/id #uuid "0a7071b6-9e18-5659-87c6-c1ca0e09122e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "005e3900-6b8d-5e21-aabf-447866db29b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467410} :answer-field/id #uuid "10ef3452-9b61-54d2-b8e0-304d34f04a95" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468426} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f985471b-d365-53ab-9bab-43f9b73d52e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467412} {:answer/id #uuid "3c3c3c75-c48d-56a2-960c-79fab11bfc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f985471b-d365-53ab-9bab-43f9b73d52e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467412} :answer-field/id #uuid "645f6342-086b-5864-b40f-faf3311eb59f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468427} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c2ecd50-6f40-5ddf-b6cc-27bce778c863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467414} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1126a1-58d2-5ef3-96eb-cf4bf898dec0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c2ecd50-6f40-5ddf-b6cc-27bce778c863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467414} :answer-field/id #uuid "977f0cda-4b4d-5298-9b59-46efd06a7e03" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa66e43c-92cc-5831-9942-3be250ef9ed8" :question/math-academy-id "q-38546" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8fdb835ed2998fae4d8afc3fd5e593bac6c72b1ee45c8b4fe01bdc4348322d1e.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$\n\nII. The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$\n\nIII. The function is continuous at $x=-1$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129148 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34aa8f4e-20f1-5dda-ac53-6eb411543897" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a4273a-8114-5443-8534-d3c0afff82d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467416} {:answer/id #uuid "170156c0-7b48-5db9-b7d9-e492492824c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07a4273a-8114-5443-8534-d3c0afff82d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467416} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7f094c7-aac1-563c-bc72-93c0ded2acc4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468429} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9361394d-88e3-5c3d-a822-f8ebe78293ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467418} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc078ca-6d4a-5eee-af95-3f80dd6dba23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc078ca-6d4a-5eee-af95-3f80dd6dba23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467419} :answer-field/id #uuid "041179be-1593-53e0-a98d-115131b994d0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468430} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52c15192-0f5c-5e02-bad9-d0b03f2006b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467420} {:answer/id #uuid "63459769-3de4-54bc-970e-84eaabef1a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63459769-3de4-54bc-970e-84eaabef1a4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467421} :answer-field/id #uuid "a212bc5e-5974-52ca-a60a-ef6e5a438cae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9ca9e56-ab61-56bb-8369-2b3458fa57a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-38581" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2c62bf5398a58cf3e27b3a47f4494fccc6d89e453685d1cd8620588c3d2bb2fa.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The coefficient of the leading term is positive.\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n- The degree of $P(x)$ is odd.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is odd, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nTherefore, statement I is false, while statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "07b63c0c-daaa-5f5b-acb3-58d6f36ee869" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Jump Discontinuity on a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "300eabc4-340c-5c3d-aeb2-845ce444c28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467422} {:answer/id #uuid "d83f5d6b-c310-5fa4-8838-8f8978fab1a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83f5d6b-c310-5fa4-8838-8f8978fab1a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467423} :answer-field/id #uuid "809ca4e9-905a-5156-b1d5-d4ce4e4cca06" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468432} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "169741b5-c91a-54f4-bc02-86818eaba819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467424} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5321df-f532-5a02-8b1b-4341a87f294c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "169741b5-c91a-54f4-bc02-86818eaba819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467424} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d534751-3db5-590e-b190-d141f3e4acb7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468433} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f1e6937-b452-55e5-b9fc-00a00b1d591b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467426} {:answer/id #uuid "bccdef66-e2a6-5586-ac1f-e6264f5d9bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f1e6937-b452-55e5-b9fc-00a00b1d591b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467426} :answer-field/id #uuid "93403f72-4436-5cda-9b11-22784905428c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54b552a9-f11b-599e-8e55-508447a23c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-38712" :question/problem "![](images/4a/4a9a1be6abdaf5104cecf7544dc77687db2892de1e3b39faab03f99b84003c03.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- It has a jump discontinuity at $x=2.$\n- It has a point discontinuity at $x=2.$\n- It is continuous at $x=2.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The function has a jump discontinuity at $x=2.$ Checking our conditions, we see that\n\n- $f(2)=2$ exists, $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ does not exist $\\,\\,\\times $\n\nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)=2,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=3.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=2$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, I is true, and II and III are false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129148 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34aa8f4e-20f1-5dda-ac53-6eb411543897" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dae4896a-777c-5d19-b424-351ccc57c7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467428} {:answer/id #uuid "e4ce7a3d-8909-50d0-8057-7992811d09bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dae4896a-777c-5d19-b424-351ccc57c7db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467428} :answer-field/id #uuid "9346ac02-a53a-5c87-a747-5328ba521eda" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468435} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce048a34-864a-584f-93d8-9775e5751ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467430} {:answer/id #uuid "4f63150c-7b4f-5094-8c6b-46f9034298f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f63150c-7b4f-5094-8c6b-46f9034298f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467431} :answer-field/id #uuid "002b7a09-05fc-5b4e-98c8-0a4181d7d5ae" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468436} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "825b611d-f9a8-53b6-8b44-10b1471a13b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467432} {:answer/id #uuid "cb51c88f-a607-5a64-a801-b316304de4ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "825b611d-f9a8-53b6-8b44-10b1471a13b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467432} :answer-field/id #uuid "c77fbfeb-1949-5e80-9ff9-7b505d8aef4b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468437}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0554fb0-029b-5c2c-8d39-a2786a1cbd89" :question/math-academy-id "q-38759" :question/problem "![](images/91/917c8111af178939316450421635ceaff2b9f3424764f891c4e2464926d4da99.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The degree of $P(x)$ is even.\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n- The coefficient of the leading term is negative.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is odd, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is positive.\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bab5c6a-f15f-5312-8be0-740e41bde8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467434} {:answer/id #uuid "8011ab83-1ae9-5f11-8342-7b42a240103f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bab5c6a-f15f-5312-8be0-740e41bde8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467434} :answer-field/id #uuid "c63fa5ab-754e-567b-9e4b-510a7a6ad162" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468438} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bc03224-7ff5-5865-b574-29adcd9ee3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467436} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd5b92b-7d63-5ddd-b688-cb1c28b1b2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bc03224-7ff5-5865-b574-29adcd9ee3e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467436} :answer-field/id #uuid "c155efcb-a5b6-53dd-8752-59e674dad3c1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468439} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "813cf431-3746-58d7-a353-84d8b6110731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467438} {:answer/id #uuid "50eb7922-e1a4-5ef4-86a3-81d24c4f9234" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "813cf431-3746-58d7-a353-84d8b6110731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467438} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa55ddc0-083f-5e90-97f6-a179bbd97f64" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "994b0436-bb09-5be1-b2e9-9e0b690f2b7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-39203" :question/problem "Suppose $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n- **I.** $b\\cdot a>0$\n- **II.** $b\\cdot a=0$\n- **III.** $a\\cdot a=0$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Simplifying the expression $(a+b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a+b\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-a\\cdot a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0$, we obtain that $-a\\cdot a<0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that none of the statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129321 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "359bc41e-1b6d-5177-9642-4f8697bc5ba0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation-Scaling Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aebd1d9b-7682-54a1-87d1-5625b9a74a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467440} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1c3ef4-6d14-5347-a96d-aa3d56907e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae1c3ef4-6d14-5347-a96d-aa3d56907e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467441} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c341505-ef51-58ef-9929-830b95c5da1b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468441} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98532d37-e0bd-582f-81e8-52bc4b117a19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467442} {:answer/id #uuid "aba55aa2-a395-5f99-8e94-cb61594c469c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aba55aa2-a395-5f99-8e94-cb61594c469c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467443} :answer-field/id #uuid "293e3409-0097-577e-a358-054e7db5377f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468442} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a054fdb-c8ac-5d69-ba2a-8a921c5c373e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467444} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cdc50f-c9ac-5a76-855f-242a9daa529e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4cdc50f-c9ac-5a76-855f-242a9daa529e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467445} :answer-field/id #uuid "30753b51-5644-5667-b969-2971c318dfb9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "005586ff-4a9c-5e53-b470-73135485f7ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-39216" :question/problem "Which of the following are rotation-scaling matrices?\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 3\\end{aligned}]$\n- **III.** $C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A rotation-scaling matrix has the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -b \\\\ b & a\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers that are not equal to zero simultaneously. Notice that the entries on the main diagonal are the same, while the antidiagonal entries have opposite signs.\n\nWith that in mind let's check each of the given matrices:\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}]$ is a rotation-scaling matrix.\n\n- $B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is a rotation-scaling matrix.\n\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is a rotation-scaling matrix.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129321 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "359bc41e-1b6d-5177-9642-4f8697bc5ba0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation-Scaling Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "730a249f-9909-593e-987f-dcb1e3654985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467446} {:answer/id #uuid "7f562f29-d90e-52f9-a7c0-0ade3faa4c2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "730a249f-9909-593e-987f-dcb1e3654985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467446} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f4fa1a9-caa6-575d-a4db-3f3150f93271" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468444} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d273d575-ee96-58bd-a8a5-dcc0d66f8b53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467448} {:answer/id #uuid "a962ee5c-cb7e-5e12-a832-bf6811118ac3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d273d575-ee96-58bd-a8a5-dcc0d66f8b53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467448} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5648ff4-d2eb-5a4c-8bce-106d5afbf1de" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468445} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76543da4-6b12-564a-8961-72a8de60a798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467450} {:answer/id #uuid "52aa4f38-4b8c-59ca-8d1e-39e4150502f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76543da4-6b12-564a-8961-72a8de60a798" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467450} :answer-field/id #uuid "012e81c7-a56a-5f6a-82c9-bf83079ac737" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "472e5539-e34f-5423-877f-1927b4b9d486" :question/math-academy-id "q-39246" :question/problem "Which of the following are rotation-scaling matrices?\n- **I.** $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]$\n- **II.** $B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -7 \\\\ -7 & -4\\end{aligned}]$\n- **III.** $C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A rotation-scaling matrix has the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & -b \\\\ b & a\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers that are not equal to zero simultaneously. Notice that the entries on the main diagonal are the same, while the antidiagonal entries have opposite signs.\n\nWith that in mind let's check each of the given matrices:\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]$  is *not* a rotation-scaling matrix since the entries on the main diagonal are not the same.\n\n- $B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -7 \\\\ -7 & -4\\end{aligned}]$ is *not* a rotation-scaling matrix since the entries on the antidiagonal do not have opposite signs.\n\n- $C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]$ is *not* a rotation-scaling matrix since the entries on the main diagonal are not the same.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "436169ad-a07f-5c25-ac9d-4c0589b9f1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467452} {:answer/id #uuid "71172c6d-69cb-5654-9de1-529b9f219d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71172c6d-69cb-5654-9de1-529b9f219d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467453} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd336a4-e888-5530-80a4-1f13ce8d051e" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468447} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7391a0f0-11c6-5e13-b5fa-5c4a81d4a16c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467454} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f48a37-f6d7-54a2-8786-46b1ef3f35b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7391a0f0-11c6-5e13-b5fa-5c4a81d4a16c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467454} :answer-field/id #uuid "32c892b1-1456-54d9-b9da-a3b642d33cca" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468448} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe9da6f9-ff11-5873-b211-7ef3a4f05b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467456} {:answer/id #uuid "c944e341-be44-513f-b567-efd54efb1959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe9da6f9-ff11-5873-b211-7ef3a4f05b3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467456} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd43aef-1a51-5e8e-bc1a-09365ae0a928" :answer-field/key "W" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33270b70-b678-53b1-8691-4ebd546544ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-39396" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n- **U.** $U={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **V.** $V={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}$\n- **W.** $W={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}},$\n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0,\\,{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0,\\,{w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=6-16+10=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0+0+0=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0+0+0=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-8+10=2\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=15-12-1=2\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133758 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41c2d289-8df5-551b-9501-3a762c67386f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About the Dot Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1db8eb7-e09f-56da-a287-35714cc28cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467458} {:answer/id #uuid "b1ff2546-2a88-5435-acbe-93df7f7eeafd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1ff2546-2a88-5435-acbe-93df7f7eeafd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467459} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba8eda63-91b1-56f5-a4df-cc1f8bc6d99c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468450} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e828117-5723-519f-b893-5316f2b3b3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467460} {:answer/id #uuid "c561fe9a-88e5-52b1-bde8-e459bbebb99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e828117-5723-519f-b893-5316f2b3b3b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467460} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d4bccf-e659-550b-b666-e63b0610397f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468451} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "721e29c5-37a8-527b-a2c2-c18d8874306e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467462} {:answer/id #uuid "9be70914-f2ac-53e2-9d6c-276ded2ea1b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "721e29c5-37a8-527b-a2c2-c18d8874306e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467462} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b258030-52f1-5a01-ae8e-9fcee2a439b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b1453d9c-0156-5211-9ae1-5e44ccac6939" :question/math-academy-id "q-40116" :question/problem "Suppose $(6a-9b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $a\\cdot a>0$\n\n- **II.** $a\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}(b\\cdot a)$\n\n- **III.** $b\\cdot a=-4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indedd, $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Simplifying the expression $(6a-9b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6a-9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (6a)\\cdot a-(9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a) & =9(b\\cdot a) \\\\ a\\cdot a & =\\frac{3}{2}(b\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=-4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6a-9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(-4) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078493 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62736299-f6d6-503f-a5d1-e1091e8b0429" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Geometric Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1057d0ab-c433-53fc-84a5-9ffb065d34b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467464} {:answer/id #uuid "339ba22e-0df0-517c-95d1-7e6077efd09c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1057d0ab-c433-53fc-84a5-9ffb065d34b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467464} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c41882d-c836-503b-8dc9-ef3e36f9bdcf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468453} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c01b25f9-e4e2-5ecf-b963-555e12dbb905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467466} {:answer/id #uuid "6bc09b19-9928-52c0-8f2a-bf84b9daf6bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c01b25f9-e4e2-5ecf-b963-555e12dbb905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467466} :answer-field/id #uuid "088b4927-cb51-5e0e-91b7-d85a0ed9f3b1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468454} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7456d2ff-df6b-523e-a46a-5cd5f5c8c23f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467468} {:answer/id #uuid "1b01a857-dc53-56a9-808d-76ab0abefd7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b01a857-dc53-56a9-808d-76ab0abefd7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467469} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7c5c6d1-7639-509f-b20e-bfa9b6e5b570" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "80009f32-0755-50c0-b5e3-ae14ffcb07ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-40282" :question/problem "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n- **I.** $1+5+25+125+⋯$\n- **II.** $\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{56}{9}+\\frac{784}{27}+⋯$\n- **III.** $0.1+0.01+0.001+0.000\\,1+⋯$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- For the geometric series $1+5+25+125+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{56}{9}+\\frac{784}{27}+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{(\\frac{4}{3})}{(\\frac{2}{7})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $0.1+0.01+0.001+0.000\\,1+⋯$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{0.01}{0.1} \\\\  & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series III converges."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115201 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef75bc93-76da-5992-8285-181b808eb7a0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Exponential Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fba6985-3012-59f9-9046-f7eb81bd2134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467470} {:answer/id #uuid "4176abbf-bd07-546f-8c5b-1cbab5b0a94b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4176abbf-bd07-546f-8c5b-1cbab5b0a94b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467471} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3b98d53-5717-5f50-8dd4-dd0c7af69429" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468456} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88ac396c-2449-52a9-a0d6-33a2b4292428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467472} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ec575c-69f5-5fb8-9972-08b07552919e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8ec575c-69f5-5fb8-9972-08b07552919e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467473} :answer-field/id #uuid "95a51358-016b-50f8-9abd-1bdef89debaa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468457} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa42429c-3d19-5a80-9479-8973b3e68f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467474} {:answer/id #uuid "5098c1b0-3b23-5a63-8473-81c712f3c23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa42429c-3d19-5a80-9479-8973b3e68f6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467474} :answer-field/id #uuid "694365a2-c4b5-5df8-91a8-0c68236bf025" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0164c43-f6ad-58eb-9330-df1855ede5c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-40556" :question/problem "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of $f(x)=-5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}+3?$\n\n- $-3$\n- $2$\n- $10$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The range of ${(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-5$ and then adding $3,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1} & >0 \\\\ -5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1} & <0 \\\\ -5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}+3 & <0+3 \\\\ f(x) & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)<3.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=-3$ and $y=2$ are  outputs of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/b2/b220b9c53bfaa49fe9b1b1c70fb9e21d08e247f44df8716846d08fd37ac2cf11.png)\n\n  \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326879 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115201 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef75bc93-76da-5992-8285-181b808eb7a0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Exponential Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be919c0-2e7e-55ba-ac96-3989376a6465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467476} {:answer/id #uuid "12d89c1a-7b91-587f-bcd6-3572509206a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12d89c1a-7b91-587f-bcd6-3572509206a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467477} :answer-field/id #uuid "b068adf9-1de1-54ce-add1-bac0f0ac7414" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468459} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b77c347b-36a4-5c6e-b52e-370b44d8a7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467478} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8d4346-33f6-59a1-b92e-7148fbd3fdf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed8d4346-33f6-59a1-b92e-7148fbd3fdf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467479} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6620f20-85ec-523b-96f2-0a064cfa262d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468460} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "992ba742-0d05-53df-85ef-a4b6b932078e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467480} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b8515a-b879-54b3-9bb0-f5d32d477ca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "992ba742-0d05-53df-85ef-a4b6b932078e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467480} :answer-field/id #uuid "07c07e13-de4b-5e64-850c-da341cdcf490" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f9f596e3-81e5-5b3c-9173-334b5d50904e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40798" :question/problem "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of  $f(x)={(1.5)}^{2x}-0.5?$ \n\n- $0$\n- $-0.2$\n- $-0.8$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The range of ${(1.5)}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{(1.5)}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{(1.5)}^{2x}>0.\n$$\n\nSubtracting  $0.5$ from the above inequality yields the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1.5)}^{2x} & >0 \\\\ {(1.5)}^{2x}-0.5 & >0-0.5 \\\\ f(x) & >-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)>-0.5.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=0$ and $y=-0.2$ are outputs of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/58/5876d2095bfd91417d2e6395f8a02ae817ebd476076bae929d79709ea7961a3e.png)\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115201 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef75bc93-76da-5992-8285-181b808eb7a0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Exponential Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b128238-89f2-56ef-a3a0-db3141972f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467482} {:answer/id #uuid "6c788197-15ab-5d92-beb7-29c4da863ea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b128238-89f2-56ef-a3a0-db3141972f7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467482} :answer-field/id #uuid "d90e7fa7-4834-5a3a-8d52-f6168385cd71" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468462} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24464fc7-7df1-50c5-bf7d-9f68fb6b25bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467484} {:answer/id #uuid "c6aef475-e72a-5111-a29c-cbb0c4fa553b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24464fc7-7df1-50c5-bf7d-9f68fb6b25bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467484} :answer-field/id #uuid "833342dc-9acd-5196-8b9d-79490883139d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468463} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "746e83e3-fbfa-5df1-b25d-9ad3c016ffe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467486} {:answer/id #uuid "d6ad510d-f360-5d5e-8992-4726772fb3a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6ad510d-f360-5d5e-8992-4726772fb3a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467487} :answer-field/id #uuid "b627265b-f826-5ac9-b981-cfad69c78894" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5188349b-4c96-553c-a9c2-bb2336ff508e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40799" :question/problem "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of $f(x)=-{(2)}^{-x}?$\n\n- $0$\n- $0.5$\n- $-0.5$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The range of ${2}^{-x}$ is\n\n$$\n{2}^{-x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-1$ yields the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1){(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ -{(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ f(x) & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)<0.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=-0.5$ is an output of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/95/95ad3043259402375e7b5822aef88d77027222a3372c2b8ab042d1b54e08666f.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82ceb6ee-967f-51f6-9562-a946e9616bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467488} {:answer/id #uuid "5a978d2b-7bde-5c45-a243-0e4e0a33fde7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82ceb6ee-967f-51f6-9562-a946e9616bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467488} :answer-field/id #uuid "f80dcb05-a2c2-516d-80fe-1ab0eed4e12b" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b08f801-3599-510d-8753-6582f23b7efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467490} {:answer/id #uuid "62d0a2f4-51a8-5771-9041-0b5950520f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b08f801-3599-510d-8753-6582f23b7efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467490} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4a18d9-f146-57c1-98ce-7671782922ed" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468466} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ed2b63-95a4-56b7-afb2-010d21ef08ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467492} {:answer/id #uuid "158e4809-5e64-50a5-af3e-ca976103a4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "158e4809-5e64-50a5-af3e-ca976103a4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467493} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bbb80cd-ffa5-5028-b638-d29609a12eae" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "324c0e93-0bc4-5958-ba8a-b87ad1b81b6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42028" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195c361c-f98a-56bc-95a9-a24d6ae95142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467494} {:answer/id #uuid "087e2b8e-167a-55dd-a33c-443fc10c0a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "087e2b8e-167a-55dd-a33c-443fc10c0a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467495} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bcb8c2f-2a00-55cd-bda8-3dffe1628a2f" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468468} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010a0770-3fce-59e2-86e4-c29d912931fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467496} {:answer/id #uuid "7127439e-6346-576e-adcf-02d5a6d602d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7127439e-6346-576e-adcf-02d5a6d602d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467497} :answer-field/id #uuid "e04e0008-7373-571f-9da6-ce0524c094b7" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468469} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33c9ca18-0830-5bb9-94a9-9ae66555b1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467498} {:answer/id #uuid "095d4e7f-7b52-523f-ae5b-6a414007ba1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33c9ca18-0830-5bb9-94a9-9ae66555b1a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467498} :answer-field/id #uuid "82277b7d-af0a-5d41-83d1-80cb091465ec" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "366fb16a-48e3-5635-add3-b8c862272224" :question/math-academy-id "q-42127" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block lower triangular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block lower triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $B$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329633 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115334 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf19e2ee-7c42-58b0-9254-5a44f315288a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Block Diagonal and Block Triangular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf81b5d0-b61e-5203-bb54-801438d3461d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467500} {:answer/id #uuid "fd171565-81f8-50d3-8a91-05948557c95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf81b5d0-b61e-5203-bb54-801438d3461d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467500} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a853d7c-2687-518d-a446-c138652f4c7e" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468471} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc4d0664-5482-5544-9e91-690f058f2d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467502} {:answer/id #uuid "12bbe01a-fe98-5ec1-a6c8-24a6cbbe1cca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc4d0664-5482-5544-9e91-690f058f2d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467502} :answer-field/id #uuid "34b3dc6c-709b-5dee-acff-ac14c1ddc707" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "825129c8-74ee-54bf-8b70-10f615c4071d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467504} {:answer/id #uuid "35dfa222-4364-5bbd-af7c-c6cfea240e47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "825129c8-74ee-54bf-8b70-10f615c4071d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467504} :answer-field/id #uuid "5535032e-f5c6-5f9b-b4e5-bbd70b524e51" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1e9c127-3ff2-5d29-89f3-9a02b595895a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42138" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are block upper triangular?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A block upper triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks below the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in the way described above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is *not* a block upper triangular matrix since it can't be partitioned in a way described above:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329652 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ecd3639-37c9-5252-aa12-89458787a945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467506} {:answer/id #uuid "4a17d94f-af1d-51db-b4a1-c3f5d3f929bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ecd3639-37c9-5252-aa12-89458787a945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467506} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdf24f07-c421-5ff2-bb73-41cf2a1bb824" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468474} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6ede3e0-89dd-5960-bddd-720db62f0e98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467508} {:answer/id #uuid "9298449a-ad9c-56e2-ac99-09c0dc4fccc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9298449a-ad9c-56e2-ac99-09c0dc4fccc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467509} :answer-field/id #uuid "c910b60c-d032-56a5-9324-9976088368c8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468475} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b966358-ec55-5272-a99d-1379768d11ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467510} {:answer/id #uuid "7421f4b3-99e2-5360-a4df-4fcdc8cb3bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7421f4b3-99e2-5360-a4df-4fcdc8cb3bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467511} :answer-field/id #uuid "5de5adf3-aa9f-52a9-9f7f-305d17cf782d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fffc6699-6d6e-50bb-8cc3-7d4f0e3f1d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-42460" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has a zero row\n- **II.** $A$ has two proportional columns\n- **III.** $A$ has two identical rows\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero row.\n\n- $A$ has two proportional columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7a447b8-7f09-5270-aca4-b17f9770d76a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467512} {:answer/id #uuid "20bcc14b-7336-54e8-a261-0dbcc7509b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20bcc14b-7336-54e8-a261-0dbcc7509b69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467513} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b661764-dcf8-5eba-bedc-e2374ffb5a83" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468477} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f27d7c7-943c-56e2-9e1a-eb7154c900ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467514} {:answer/id #uuid "9113697f-b704-5925-b69c-e204a21d502a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f27d7c7-943c-56e2-9e1a-eb7154c900ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467514} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba64ddd8-bbc6-577f-b73b-e524ed587e49" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468478} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68448d61-0ddf-531f-8009-f672e592a9b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467516} {:answer/id #uuid "84b46424-4893-5f87-bbc8-ae085db91a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68448d61-0ddf-531f-8009-f672e592a9b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467516} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2a724bd-e000-5d5f-b930-fed8c566efc4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59d4edee-acd9-59e0-80f8-ec390e2e0ee0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42465" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nII. $A$ has identical columns\n\nIII. $A$ has a zero column\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have a zero column.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be7744ec-227d-555c-b802-95392ec513c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467518} {:answer/id #uuid "f886a11b-86a7-5b5a-8f76-6da328b63714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f886a11b-86a7-5b5a-8f76-6da328b63714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467519} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d7c76e-d109-5769-8668-62038090a469" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b1e6c3-5e63-57c4-9a2c-3c91c2d3c235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467520} {:answer/id #uuid "0e0f888e-4bbc-5ac8-806d-7f7a885bfed4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b1e6c3-5e63-57c4-9a2c-3c91c2d3c235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467520} :answer-field/id #uuid "14df28d2-7f17-512c-aa78-54fedf4382f1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d8c2352-983b-5658-8df2-16e409639b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467522} {:answer/id #uuid "a3313dd9-a767-59cb-bba4-c976f1f2ec54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8c2352-983b-5658-8df2-16e409639b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467522} :answer-field/id #uuid "1283c815-0425-57c4-8ea5-2495c255615f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cc386e74-2622-5d48-a383-9789d25d9007" :question/math-academy-id "q-42613" :question/problem "Let $⟨-4,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9x+11y=-14 \\\\ 6x-ky=-34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=-4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 1 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- **III.** $-4|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ -4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79b0b35e-3c5e-57bc-8aaf-dc4fa16cdba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467524} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd1b03b-3c8d-5a6e-b684-80444b0cc678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bd1b03b-3c8d-5a6e-b684-80444b0cc678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467525} :answer-field/id #uuid "de3db739-254c-5821-80ad-9acd32e361f9" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468483} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c3a9014-5808-53b0-ab98-c0cca13bf13b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467526} {:answer/id #uuid "c13400aa-3d88-5366-908f-9f7fffe2af9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c13400aa-3d88-5366-908f-9f7fffe2af9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467527} :answer-field/id #uuid "e25f4dac-42f6-5106-9850-ab4e5c087959" :answer-field/key "Q" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7191e2a0-f178-5d00-aec5-334b5b5b342d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467528} {:answer/id #uuid "b4484943-328e-5ce9-9d28-9a215a0a7fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7191e2a0-f178-5d00-aec5-334b5b5b342d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467528} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd3c5d47-0088-54ee-b2a3-b8323cc401fa" :answer-field/key "W" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9df20933-ebce-545d-be35-aa9a6fe179d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42751" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $Q$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =Q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $W$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $Q$ and $E$ are elementary matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62c719e0-d25a-59ec-a391-67f41278bccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467530} {:answer/id #uuid "849fb659-4d9a-5640-b741-4b42c0a2fe08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62c719e0-d25a-59ec-a391-67f41278bccc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467530} :answer-field/id #uuid "5936cb4f-6ef1-5007-8ddb-e8fa3ea9a73e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58ddd5cd-f2b6-5fce-9e50-51af7059d7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467532} {:answer/id #uuid "4eccff29-5dd8-5062-bdc3-d964a3b204b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58ddd5cd-f2b6-5fce-9e50-51af7059d7a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3481d3b-57f8-5225-b91c-3c0be05b7ac7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468487} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a03323e1-ad31-55cd-86ab-f5fa0debeb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467534} {:answer/id #uuid "926a9028-0022-5d33-98e5-63757d49eabb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "926a9028-0022-5d33-98e5-63757d49eabb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467535} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c53ddf1-c2d8-545a-bdb3-ed7c844e7094" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "84d0f456-e91d-5ae9-ab2b-9060640f7227" :question/math-academy-id "q-42853" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=sec⁡x?$\n- **I.** $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain.\n- **II.** $x=\\pi $ is a root. $$\n- **III.** $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ is not in the range of the function.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](images/da/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ thus it is not defined for $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has no zeros.\n\n- Statement III is true. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ does not belong to the range."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b39f5b-1a9f-5406-a6a3-ca922728ac21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467536} {:answer/id #uuid "a82257d2-6939-5094-b209-8c3f8a6ca528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b39f5b-1a9f-5406-a6a3-ca922728ac21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467536} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa7fb85-2e34-51b0-801e-44fdce823bfd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "334b114b-89c0-5778-85fc-b19d61115037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467538} {:answer/id #uuid "dcbb6570-b38c-51d8-8e6d-983c8121bded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcbb6570-b38c-51d8-8e6d-983c8121bded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467539} :answer-field/id #uuid "6155eda5-776d-536c-9839-c334c3fbac7d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46873272-c960-50c8-a66f-af2707c5c86b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467540} {:answer/id #uuid "d2864d48-61db-5ab1-a2bd-c0aa7dc3c175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2864d48-61db-5ab1-a2bd-c0aa7dc3c175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467541} :answer-field/id #uuid "250be72e-dcdb-5259-b3b8-15930933244e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3923a242-a394-5f37-9f6d-741dafd435c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42886" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x?$\n\nI. The point $(0,2)$ is in the graph\n\nII. $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote\n\nIII. $y=-2$ belongs to the range of the function.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](images/da/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The $y$-intercept of $sec⁡x$ is $1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function $y=sec⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ thus $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote.\n\n- Statement III is true. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=-2$ belongs to the range."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4afd7480-9ba2-5374-a72a-1ce388431ec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467542} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1541c0-ce3a-5729-bd28-e3be94a41d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4afd7480-9ba2-5374-a72a-1ce388431ec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467542} :answer-field/id #uuid "85527b57-8432-57dc-bed5-c02a16abd64c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468492} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8508e63a-a336-5f33-b33d-1465eccaf904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467544} {:answer/id #uuid "077ab677-6583-55ce-a7e6-6af8b1fa9881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "077ab677-6583-55ce-a7e6-6af8b1fa9881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467545} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9cbc72f-04da-5ebd-99d5-d87d09aca807" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468493} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88126427-956a-5315-9096-9099252df5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467546} {:answer/id #uuid "a49d1e0b-d87d-5990-9f1d-19472bb6081c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a49d1e0b-d87d-5990-9f1d-19472bb6081c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467547} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5dbf19f-117b-5de5-8d38-1828f362ece6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f48e886-80d4-5268-94be-6547f7232323" :question/math-academy-id "q-42957" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n- **I.** $A$ has identical columns\n- **II.** $A$ has a zero column\n- **III.** $A$ has identical rows\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35563308-1bf5-5412-b3ac-38e945d6435f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467548} {:answer/id #uuid "8cce9941-e08e-5b25-878b-8a3e1fd19b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35563308-1bf5-5412-b3ac-38e945d6435f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467548} :answer-field/id #uuid "14870e3e-adcd-5e31-8d98-7270ab6e02ba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c55623-fcd2-5073-8bbe-89c8cd4a2e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467550} {:answer/id #uuid "79d4acc9-9024-588c-a500-b68af6d2d348" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02c55623-fcd2-5073-8bbe-89c8cd4a2e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467550} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa0e6660-67a9-5431-b123-e8f58681f385" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c20d9fe-a802-5cb2-97e5-b29befe6b81d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467552} {:answer/id #uuid "99913413-aa5b-526c-8205-7d8f2623301b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99913413-aa5b-526c-8205-7d8f2623301b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467553} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d0e47a0-8744-5d99-932d-e825a9175d73" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "854132a3-b7f0-5d3e-b0d4-55e43fe2b0f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-42984" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y=k \\\\ 2x-y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-13$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-1$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=13$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3-10 \\\\  & -13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|}{-13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)(-13) \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Closed Under Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba58b671-2657-5a03-abe7-c1d0f53623a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467554} {:answer/id #uuid "ba1c3ce4-672a-5a3c-a83d-bb611ddd59bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba1c3ce4-672a-5a3c-a83d-bb611ddd59bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467555} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c5d2488-f6b5-5b00-8662-08305a2ef8b5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468498} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40ba87ba-c6e2-5de6-b649-e0483026a236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467556} {:answer/id #uuid "62f2e689-0881-5c43-bed6-64a96561cc4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40ba87ba-c6e2-5de6-b649-e0483026a236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467556} :answer-field/id #uuid "a50d472b-7d51-5fe0-859e-60a2e6abcfa4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468499} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54074d74-4264-5c20-8484-753531648f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467558} {:answer/id #uuid "e7263bac-9438-5bd2-bceb-9ddd2ae62b91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54074d74-4264-5c20-8484-753531648f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467558} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e58aa32-3f2c-58e2-a22d-6bae8ee75a9b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4fc2576-da47-56c9-aeca-80fed8de957c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43859" :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $q(x)\\in W,$ where $q(x)={2}^{x}.$\n- **II.** For any $f(x)\\in W$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot f(x)\\in W.$\n- **III.** The set is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q(x)={2}^{x}\\in W$ because\n\n$$\nq(0)={2}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. There exists a function in $W$ that has a scalar multiple *not* in $W.$ For example, let $f(x)={2}^{x}$ and $k=2.$ Notice that $f(x)$ belongs to $W$ since $f(0)=1.$ However,\n\n$$\n2\\cdot f(0)=2\\cdot {2}^{0}=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nHence, $k\\cdot f(x)\\notin W.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133957 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1012ae9a-26d6-50bf-a46a-7c859d856752" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals On Which the IVT Can Be Applied"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c7405ea-c98b-5325-b63e-2807e36d76d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467560} {:answer/id #uuid "26e98b7e-56f8-5b47-b85d-e433904b1fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26e98b7e-56f8-5b47-b85d-e433904b1fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467561} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d2f07a7-b601-54ee-9407-23b9e2e1ccad" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd77ad93-91ef-5c0f-a754-61403fd2b082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467562} {:answer/id #uuid "3310ece2-aa6d-5452-bfaa-6e91380d4455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd77ad93-91ef-5c0f-a754-61403fd2b082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467562} :answer-field/id #uuid "66a80203-6b00-5a67-8ab9-e11f7f67970b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468502} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8378235-3099-5770-a4cf-2dbdf0e69e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467564} {:answer/id #uuid "f922edc2-68b0-5ca7-8e60-d2d9f9ab5036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8378235-3099-5770-a4cf-2dbdf0e69e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467564} :answer-field/id #uuid "3698a02e-a636-58f8-a9a1-b0ab2791efd5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "09a3da32-3de0-5834-befe-e2cd86cc2a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-47016" :question/problem "Consider the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ On which of the following intervals can the intermediate value theorem be applied to this function?\n- **I.** $[0,1]$\n- **II.** $[1,2]$\n- **III.** $[-1,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The intermediate value theorem can be applied on closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nThe function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}$ is discontinuous at the values of $x$ which make the denominator $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ equal to zero. Therefore, $f(x)$ is discontinuous at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $, where $n$ is any integer.\n\n- On the interval $[0,1],$ we **can** apply the intermediate value theorem to $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- On the interval $[1,2],$ we **cannot** apply the intermediate value theorem to $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ because this interval contains the point of discontinuity $\\frac{\\pi }{2}≈1.57\\,.$\n\n- On the interval $[-1,0),$ we **cannot** apply the intermediate value theorem to $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ because this interval is not closed.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329801 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133957 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1012ae9a-26d6-50bf-a46a-7c859d856752" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals On Which the IVT Can Be Applied"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9571fe0-bef8-5f1e-9ba0-4c06a4b482c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467566} {:answer/id #uuid "4766a3dd-ffe7-58c7-97d9-8370199dc6e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4766a3dd-ffe7-58c7-97d9-8370199dc6e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467567} :answer-field/id #uuid "990578cb-68f3-5bff-ac55-4c4c35ea5506" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a11a4707-8927-586b-bc26-719ddc4f1372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467568} {:answer/id #uuid "47dbafb2-cabc-51dc-9055-c385426b609f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a11a4707-8927-586b-bc26-719ddc4f1372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467568} :answer-field/id #uuid "0126cb1a-d5b7-51f6-b9cd-d2b08e3e2f66" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468505} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "219820d5-c88c-55a4-9c0c-7ab18afb9233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467570} {:answer/id #uuid "55fd1b5c-e37f-51f0-b8af-339da920860d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "219820d5-c88c-55a4-9c0c-7ab18afb9233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467570} :answer-field/id #uuid "e605a49f-dffa-50b2-9558-b152728ee5ef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2fde248b-aec3-5f7a-8ce9-4a20cf4e8153" :question/math-academy-id "q-47035" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=x(x+3)(x-2).$ On which of the following intervals does the intermediate value theorem guarantee that the equation $f(x)=-5$ has a solution?\n- **I.** $[-5,-3]$\n- **II.** $[-3,-2]$\n- **III.** $[-2,0]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $f(x)$ is a polynomial, it's continuous over the real numbers. Thus, we can apply the intermediate value theorem to any of the given intervals.\n\nLet's make a table with the values of $f(x)$ at the endpoints.\n\n| $x$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $-70$ | $0$ | $8$ | $0$ |\n\n- On the interval $[-5,-3],$ we have $f(-5)=-70$ and $f(-3)=0.$ Since $-5\\in [-70,0],$ the IVT does guarantee a solution to the equation $f(x)=-5$ on this interval.\n\n- On the interval $[-3,-2],$ we have $f(-3)=0$ and $f(-2)=8.$ Since $-5\\notin [0,8],$ the IVT does *not* guarantee a solution to the equation $f(x)=-5$ on this interval.\n\n- On the interval $[-2,0],$ we have $f(-2)=8$ and $f(0)=0.$ Since $-5\\notin [0,8],$ the IVT does *not* guarantee a solution to the equation $f(x)=-5$ on this interval.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133957 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1012ae9a-26d6-50bf-a46a-7c859d856752" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals On Which the IVT Can Be Applied"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f344881-385c-5665-85eb-bf009723e051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467572} {:answer/id #uuid "b0338624-0f00-542b-ad9e-7189e7be0ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f344881-385c-5665-85eb-bf009723e051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467572} :answer-field/id #uuid "267d92af-d407-5c35-ac8f-a6c162abe01d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468507} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0eccd15-4643-594c-9b76-cc1f8b6669b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467574} {:answer/id #uuid "acfa8399-1619-5e81-b743-8ccb518c5111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acfa8399-1619-5e81-b743-8ccb518c5111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467575} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e6b3564-dbb4-56c7-a3c8-0f7852ea53a6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468508} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ddc250d-3035-5ac8-aff3-71357621fce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467576} {:answer/id #uuid "57d257e8-63d5-5cd3-990e-9061ae7ffc99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ddc250d-3035-5ac8-aff3-71357621fce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467576} :answer-field/id #uuid "054c1693-cd72-59a0-8e2f-778669cf35f6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ee052f2c-7f8b-5e1c-a710-1b1e4c2963cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-47055" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{x-2}.$ In which of the following intervals does the intermediate value theorem guarantee that the equation $f(x)=3$ has a solution? \n- **I.** $[-4,-1]$\n- **II.** $[3,5]$\n- **III.** $[-1,4]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)=\\frac{x+1}{x-2}$ is discontinuous at the values of $x$ which make the denominator equal to zero. Therefore, $f(x)$ is discontinuous at $x=2,$ and so the intermediate value theorem can be applied to the function $f(x)$ only on closed intervals that do not contain the point $x=2$ \n\nLet's make a table with the values of $f(x)$ at the endpoints.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0$ | $4$ | $2.5$ | $2$ |\n\n- On the interval $[-4,-1],$ we have $f(-4)=0.5$ and $f(-1)=0.$ Since $3\\notin [0,0.5],$ the IVT does *not* guarantee a solution to the equation $f(x)=3$ on this interval.\n\n- On the interval $[3,5],$ we have $f(3)=4$ and $f(5)=2.$ Since $3\\in [2,4],$ the IVT *does* guarantee a solution to the equation $f(x)=3$ on this interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,4]$ contains the point $x=2.$ Therefore we can not apply the intermediate value theorem on this interval.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II  only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86d1fafe-67a4-5304-b42b-0fa34a95eaff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467578} {:answer/id #uuid "c76c9ea4-d5d0-5c09-adc5-db52b1568fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c76c9ea4-d5d0-5c09-adc5-db52b1568fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467579} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df948ff-c1ab-538f-b99e-ed07682677fc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6428bf6c-1cd8-523e-89a2-bbd6aefca97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} {:answer/id #uuid "49e7f113-867c-5ee0-a738-ba5b88651827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6428bf6c-1cd8-523e-89a2-bbd6aefca97b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467580} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e8c77e6-a0b4-526b-bf8e-a435b7b66ac1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b22f319-2182-5f2f-984d-2c69a38c95bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} {:answer/id #uuid "f8184f79-583b-5721-92be-e461d3dc1a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b22f319-2182-5f2f-984d-2c69a38c95bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467582} :answer-field/id #uuid "d58f3fca-628f-5dd4-9837-348f91ad595e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c600e13-fdff-5526-82d0-6659ac10dfc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-47587" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ has no inverse\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times $\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115236 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b2036f-da0f-59de-8a39-6b33e6cbdd04" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a True Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6943c140-8ce8-5ef3-a24a-ec4dd3989d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467584} {:answer/id #uuid "f903da43-b955-557b-b07e-9a56a9cb9411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f903da43-b955-557b-b07e-9a56a9cb9411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467585} :answer-field/id #uuid "131a190d-2e93-5c45-8f99-0ed790058e01" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a3ed0f-3e98-54bf-9262-acf83b1ca310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467586} {:answer/id #uuid "ce418b35-cc2f-53d8-bacf-bc6a8f351d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce418b35-cc2f-53d8-bacf-bc6a8f351d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467587} :answer-field/id #uuid "71011c6f-48e1-5eb7-add1-32fab707cd37" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468514} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "801e1932-e9a9-5a2e-a418-1e17c385bb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467588} {:answer/id #uuid "6016d1b1-b380-5755-a999-dcec788a69fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "801e1932-e9a9-5a2e-a418-1e17c385bb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467588} :answer-field/id #uuid "559e34e0-cb19-5844-a24f-bc87f0e1438e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffbb2a4c-595d-59cc-bffd-a39a18b105b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-47657" :question/problem "Which of the following completes the statement so that it is true:\n\n*If the unique solution of $Ax=0,$ where $A$ is a $2\\times 2$-matrix, is $⟨0,0⟩$, then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n- **I.** $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n- **III.** ${A}^{-1}$ does not exist\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.  \n\nNow, since the third part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem, only options I and II give us true statements:\n\n- *If the unique solution of $Ax=0$ is $⟨0,0⟩$, then $det(A)\\ne 0$ .* $\\,✓$\n\n- *If the unique solution of $Ax=0$ is $⟨0,0⟩$, then $A$ is invertible .*$\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eede91c4-9099-55df-a803-f87895d9f51b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extreme Value Theorem to Piecewise Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cc37e5f-628a-5453-b9aa-5f7736bbc9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467590} {:answer/id #uuid "86c33542-1a37-5a8c-829b-f0ce4c00b10a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cc37e5f-628a-5453-b9aa-5f7736bbc9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467590} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2c6904f-d234-579f-a1ce-7aceea241e6b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468516} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b766daf9-f662-5b41-bf41-146b6ff13df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467592} {:answer/id #uuid "ffeccce2-717e-5e80-b3c0-db1259995cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffeccce2-717e-5e80-b3c0-db1259995cf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467593} :answer-field/id #uuid "814f8eea-219e-55ac-a376-98a938bdbd22" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468517} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7babf862-7892-5b69-9b8c-2026a9d0a99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467594} {:answer/id #uuid "61ed1c67-3d18-527d-aa8b-5e81455211be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7babf862-7892-5b69-9b8c-2026a9d0a99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467594} :answer-field/id #uuid "95cc6ec8-9bed-5ab7-9e0d-2ce973417c1a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a410e5f1-db4f-5d99-8a2f-cd16595bdd74" :question/math-academy-id "q-47923" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x}, & x\\ne 0 \\\\ \\,\\,1, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function?\n- **I.** $[-1,1]$\n- **II.** $[0.5,1]$\n- **III.** $[-1,0)$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nSo, let's check whether the function is continuous on each of the intervals. \n\n- Let first consider the interval  $[-1,1].$ This is a  closed interval, but we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{x}=\\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ has an essential discontinuity at $x=0.$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous on the interval $[-1,1]$, and the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- Now consider  $[0.5,1].$ The only discontinuity of the function $f(x)$ is at $x=0,$ which is not in the interval  $[0.5,1].$ Therefore, $f(x)$ is continuous on the interval  $[0.5,1],$ and the extreme value theorem is applicable on this interval.\n\n- Finally, we note that the interval $[-1,0)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable in this case.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}]}
